---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility Statement | A-Worthy Singapore Tuition" description="How A-Worthy works to meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA so every student and parent can use our website: what we support, known limits, and how to send us feedback.">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container a11y-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Accessibility</span>
      <h1 class="a11y-title squiggle">Accessibility statement&nbsp;&mdash; <span class="nowrap">A-Worthy</span> Singapore</h1>

      <p>We want everyone to be able to use our website, including people with disabilities. We work to meet the <strong>WCAG 2.2 Level AA</strong> standard.</p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic HTML with proper heading hierarchy</li>
        <li>ARIA labels on all interactive elements</li>
        <li>Keyboard navigation support throughout the site</li>
        <li>Sufficient colour contrast ratios in both light and dark modes</li>
        <li>Reduced motion support for users who prefer less animation</li>
        <li>High contrast mode compatibility</li>
        <li>Screen reader compatible content structure</li>
        <li>Skip-to-content link for keyboard users</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <p>Some of our PDF resources may not work fully with screen readers, and we&rsquo;re working on that. When we add video, it will have captions.</p>

      <h2>Feedback</h2>
      <p>If anything on our website is hard to use or doesn&rsquo;t work with your assistive technology, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. We read all feedback and will work to fix the problem promptly.</p>

      <p class="a11y-updated">This statement was last updated in April 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* 45rem = 720px up to 1440px; in rem so the measure grows with the root
     size at >=1441px (a px cap left ~55-character lines and a 3-line h1 on
     1920/2560 screens once the type had scaled up) */
  .a11y-content {
    max-width: 45rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .a11y-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  /* Keep the em dash on line 1 and never split "A-Worthy" at its hyphen */
  .a11y-title .nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .a11y-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .a11y-content ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .a11y-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .a11y-content a {
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }
  .a11y-updated {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
